## 7. Build Your Workflow + Close

---

### ACTIVITY — Activity 2: Build Your Workflow
- Pill: ACTIVITY
- Title: Set up your folder. Pick your tool. Run one prompt.
- Lead: Use your Activity 1 canvas. Use your real project.
- 🎨 Visual hint: Same plain treatment as the other Activity slides — white background, orange-outline "ACTIVITY" pill, bold instruction, no timer, no diagram. Keep this one text-only; the mint-green AI-prompt card belongs on the next slide instead, since this activity's prompt depends on what the student picks.

---

### PRACTICE — AI in Practice
- Kicker: AI in Practice
- Title: Write a CARE prompt — then audit yourself
- AI prompt card: *"I'm a UX designer working on [project], at the [stage] stage. Using CARE, write a prompt for [task]. Then critique it: what's ambiguous, what should I add?"*
- Critical thinking: Did the self-critique catch something you missed? Where does it still leave a decision to AI that should be yours?
- 🎨 Visual hint: The pale mint-green AI-prompt card component, exactly as used throughout the reference deck's Assignment slides — bold italic "🤖 AI in Practice — Paste this prompt into AI tools:" header, prompt in italic below, white background around the card. Not a dark monospace card — match the reference deck's actual style.

---

### ASSIGNMENT 1 — Set Up Your AI Workflow
- Pill: ASSIGNMENT 1
- Title: Set up your AI workflow
- Bullets (purple dots):
  - Local folder created and organised, using one of the three options from earlier
  - Primary AI chat tool chosen as your default for the rest of the program
  - Prompt library started — 3+ CARE-structured prompts
- Footer line: *If you finished Activity 2 in class, this is mostly about finishing and documenting it properly.*
- 🎨 Visual hint: Matches the reference deck's individual assignment slides exactly — white background, orange-outline "ASSIGNMENT 1" pill top-left, bold black title, purple-bullet-dot list, no AI-prompt card needed on this one (it's a setup task, not a prompting task).

---

### ASSIGNMENT 2 — Capture & Organise Your Current Screens
- Pill: ASSIGNMENT 2
- Title: Capture your current screens
- Bullets (purple dots):
  - For each key experience, capture the current screen flow as it exists today
  - Screenshot each screen — high-level overview, not every micro-state
  - Save into your Assignment 1 folder, labelled by state
  - We will use these flows next session to set up friction metrics
- AI prompt card: *"Here is my screen flow: [describe or paste]. Draft a one-line label for each screen — what it is and what state it's in."*
- 🎨 Visual hint: Same individual-assignment treatment — orange-outline "ASSIGNMENT 2" pill, bold title, purple-bullet list, and the mint-green AI-prompt card at the bottom of the same slide, matching the reference deck's Assignment 2 and 3 slides exactly.

---

### END — Closing *(optional — the reference deck has no equivalent slide; add only if you want a deliberate close rather than ending on Assignment 2)*
- Kicker: One thing to carry forward
- Title: "The tool will\nkeep changing.\n*This workflow won't.*"
- Lead: Define clearly. Prompt deliberately. Review critically.
- Sign: — Winnie Nguyen
- 🎨 Visual hint: Plain white background, large stacked title lines, last line in iris/purple. No diagram — quiet, minimal, in keeping with the reference deck's restrained style even though the reference deck itself doesn't have this slide.
